icrofreak/Preset/077 Eonz",["Updated"]],["p-13b82eb33ec77002.html","source-block-636","ChatGPT/Sites/Q/To what extent is it possible, either using Claude artifacts or using ChatGPT sites, to have a database that backs the site?",["Updated"]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-0","My Thoughts",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-20","I intend to use local mounts backed by Backblaze/B2 for assets, with relative local paths in garden source pages. At publish time, both the Logseq site pipeline and GitP/A's publishing pipeline should transform those paths into stable Cloudflare CDN URLs in the published output, including episode pages and RSS media enclosures.",["My Thoughts"]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-361","TIL",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-371","In Claude Enterprise, a private project can include data imported from a GitHub repository, but in my org an org-wide project has that option disabled. It looks like a one-time import, and I haven't found an easy way to refresh it yet, though I haven't tried. See Claude/Project/Explanation/How the GitHub integration feeds project knowledge and the official Use the GitHub integration article.",["TIL"]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-865","Cloudflare/D1",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-886","Cloudflare/R2",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-907","Cloudflare/R2/Concept/Pricing Compared with Backblaze B2",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-971","Claude/Project/Explanation/How the GitHub integration feeds project knowledge",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-1056","Claude/Project/Q/What is the limit on the capacity for adding knowledge to a Claude project?",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-1156","Claude/Project/RAG",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-1182","Claude/Artifact/Concept/Install as Desktop App",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-1236","Updated",[]],["p-1431f5dd2442fd63.html","source-block-125